!!! 03-control-flow.matrix
!!! Conditionals, every loop form, and pattern consideration.
!!!
!!! Every loop opens with "repeat" and closes with "end repeat", so a loop
!!! terminator can never be matched to the wrong loop kind.

book tour.flow

classify receives count as number returns text begin paragraph
    when count is greater than 0 then
        give "positive"
    otherwise when count is less than 0 then
        give "negative"
    otherwise
        give "zero"
    end when
end paragraph

main returns number begin paragraph

    say classify with count being 7

    !!! Condition-first loop.
    variable index as number is 0
    repeat while index is less than 5
        say index
        set index to index plus 1
    end repeat

    !!! Counted loop. "from 0 to 5" visits 0 through 4, matching Ny's
    !!! exclusive range.
    repeat for step from 0 to 5
        when step equals 3 then
            continue repeating
        end when
        say step
    end repeat

    !!! Iteration over an array.
    value names as array of text is ["alpha", "beta", "gamma"]
    repeat for each name in names
        say name
    end repeat

    !!! Unbounded loop with an explicit exit.
    variable budget as number is 3
    repeat forever
        when budget is at most 0 then
            stop repeating
        end when
        set budget to budget minus 1
    end repeat

    !!! Statement-form consideration. "otherwise" is the wildcard arm.
    value code as number is 2
    consider code
        when 1 then say "one"
        when 2 then say "two"
        otherwise say "other"
    end consider

    !!! Both conditional forms also produce values. In value position the
    !!! branches say "give", because "give" always marks the value leaving
    !!! the construct the reader is inside -- a function, an arm, a branch.
    !!! It also makes Ny's rule a parse rule: an expression arm is exactly one
    !!! expression, so a statement block cannot accidentally appear where a
    !!! value is required.
    value sign as number is when code is greater than 0 give 1 otherwise give minus 1 end when
    value word as text is consider code
        when 1 give "one"
        when 2 give "two"
        otherwise give "other"
    end consider

    say sign
    say word
    give 0
end paragraph
